  desc: in Minesweeper's help, moving the cursor with the iPod's buttons: keep ◀ and ▶ as they are, and Menu and Play as the iPod's own phrases name those buttons
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Turn the wheel to go through the field square by square, or press ◀, ▶, Menu and Play to move left, right, up and down."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "轉動轉盤可逐格移動，或按 ◀、▶、Menu 和 Play 向左、右、上、下移動。"
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_MINESWEEPER_HELP_SELECT
  desc: in Minesweeper's help: a short press of the iPod's centre button flags a square, holding it opens the square; Select as the iPod's own phrases name that button
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Press Select to put a flag on a square you think hides a mine, and again to take it off. Hold Select to open the square."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "按下 Select 在你認為有地雷的方格上插旗子，再按一次取消。按住 Select 打開方格。"
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
<phrase>
  id: LANG_MINESWEEPER_HELP_MORE
  desc: in Minesweeper's help, the last paragraph: the counts shown by Select and Play pressed together, leaving the game with Select and Menu together, and the field shown after a game
  user: extras
  <source>
    *: "Once a square is open, press Select and Play together to see how many flags you've placed and how many mines there are. Press Select and Menu together to leave Minesweeper. When a game ends, the whole field shows; press any button to go back to the menu."
  </source>
  <dest>
    *: "打開方格後，同時按下 Select 和 Play 可查看已插的旗子數和地雷總數。同時按下 Select 和 Menu 可離開踩地雷。遊戲結束時會顯示整個雷區，按任一按鈕返回選單。"
  </dest>
  <voice>
    *: ""
  </voice>
</phrase>
